{"id": "EUVD-2026-93114", "enisaUuid": "be1f50e9-5605-320e-861f-e5d2f04297bc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mwifiex: bound the pairwise-cipher OUI walk to the IE length\n\nmwifiex_search_oui_in_ie() reads a pairwise-cipher (PTK) count from a\nbeacon/probe-response RSN or WPA information element and then walks that\nmany 4-byte OUIs, comparing each with memcmp(). The count comes straight\nfrom the (attacker-supplied) IE and is never checked against the\nelement's own length, and the callers admit the element on element_id\nalone (has_ieee_hdr() / has_vendor_hdr(), no length check). A crafted\nRSN/WPA IE with a large pairwise count therefore makes the walk read up\nto 255 * 4 bytes past the element -- an out-of-bounds read of the\nkmemdup()'d beacon buffer, reachable from any AP whose beacon/probe\nresponse is processed during scan-result parsing.\n\nPass the number of IE bytes available at the OUI list and bound the walk\nto the element. Keep the length signed and reject a negative value\nbefore any unsigned arithmetic, so a small or zero IE length cannot\nunderflow to a large size_t and defeat the bound.\n\nFound by 0sec automated security-research tooling (https://0sec.ai).", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77e642af7f2f6029e12a35c847c56cbd0466e799", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/982b8fcdbb28f63bbbf02f0822c0bbda12ec27ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58767b41f87244eebaa5a475b9d276c83b89b933", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2402c9e2644b7e10c7aaaf87bf12743d7e363559", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54a9cc5bd70b0d77a5069d4c46998c679a10c857", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8bbef2b1ebfbadc0b9c37bbbf9c9e26fe2e41960", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46cda9d42f0d6ec3057d878ddb1f38c0ab9f51df", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e667aee1c192d67d27c803007bfa9c6e0873e959"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98186", "GHSA-vmvq-5qrr-gvg2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c168735-de05-326b-b718-8f2c8099fcc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6e3a92b9a4c9416b17f468fa5c7fa2233b8b4e <8bbef2b1ebfbadc0b9c37bbbf9c9e26fe2e41960"}, {"id": "1dd4a607-8255-3a51-bf33-c4da7a92a445", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "1efb70f2-6122-36a3-adec-5fcecb156322", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6e3a92b9a4c9416b17f468fa5c7fa2233b8b4e <982b8fcdbb28f63bbbf02f0822c0bbda12ec27ed"}, {"id": "239ed93e-18ca-3629-9d9c-f640a9568d70", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6e3a92b9a4c9416b17f468fa5c7fa2233b8b4e <46cda9d42f0d6ec3057d878ddb1f38c0ab9f51df"}, {"id": "38ff1b80-acbe-30d1-ac0c-0f3528df8c95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.0"}, {"id": "3e4f1c58-85c1-3d6b-ac54-c772f3b41fb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "3f6524ef-65a5-3de9-99f6-29701c7d0fe3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "477bad00-9306-32a1-b810-126f192bfe1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6e3a92b9a4c9416b17f468fa5c7fa2233b8b4e <77e642af7f2f6029e12a35c847c56cbd0466e799"}, {"id": "7210b767-6372-3aa0-a102-af11c10c1113", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6e3a92b9a4c9416b17f468fa5c7fa2233b8b4e <54a9cc5bd70b0d77a5069d4c46998c679a10c857"}, {"id": "78fb63ba-dd1b-34df-99f1-1cd0e3521b32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7f6439b0-9780-3b1a-aba7-710590cfabc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5e6e3a92b9a4c9416b17f4